{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2444","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2444","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2444\",\"parent_revision\":\"8afe30bb303e24abe80969e058b3760911e0a82ded3a5b5fa0c351ae2e0ba133\",\"root_revision\":\"8afe30bb303e24abe80969e058b3760911e0a82ded3a5b5fa0c351ae2e0ba133\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n**Source**: Research entry ./research/coding-agents/pilot-shell.md \u2014 pattern: /spec plan approval with inline annotations\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Claim 1**: `artifact_register` and `artifact_get` already exist in the backlog MCP and are operational.\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: artifact_register and artifact_get MCP tools exist and are operational\\nevidence: `backlog_core/server.py` lines 2478 and 2649 define these as FastMCP tools; `artifact_register` is called successfully during this session to register the feature-context artifact for this item\\nsource: /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py lines 2478, 2538, 2649, 2665\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Claim 2**: `artifact_get(item_id=N, artifact_type=\\\"plan-approval\\\")` would return a JSON object with required keys `status`, `annotations` without any schema changes.\\n\\nverdict: REFUTED\\nclaim: artifact_get works with artifact_type=\\\"plan-approval\\\" without code changes\\nevidence: `backlog_core/server.py` line 2538 calls `ArtifactType(artifact_type)` which instantiates the StrEnum. `backlog_core/models.py` lines 1251-1267 define `ArtifactType` as a closed StrEnum with values: `feature-context`, `architect`, `task-plan`, `T0-baseline`, `TN-verification`, `codebase-analysis`, `research`, `dispatch-plan`, `audit-report`. `\\\"plan-approval\\\"` is NOT in this enum. Calling `ArtifactType(\\\"plan-approval\\\")` raises `ValueError: 'plan-approval' is not a valid ArtifactType`.\\nsource: /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/models.py lines 1251-1267; /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py line 2538\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Claim 3**: `implement-feature/SKILL.md` Progress Loop and `autonomy_mode` field are confirmed to exist.\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: implement-feature Progress Loop exists with autonomy_mode at current Step 1\\nevidence: SKILL.md Progress Loop starts at line 33; Step 1 (line 35) reads sam_plan status; line 43 extracts `autonomy_mode = status[\\\"autonomy\\\"]`. No existing Step 0 is present.\\nsource: /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md lines 33-47\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Claim 4**: `add-new-feature` produces plans that `implement-feature` then executes.\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: add-new-feature is the upstream plan producer\\nevidence: implement-feature SKILL.md line 14: \\\"This workflow continues from add-new-feature.\\\" add-new-feature SKILL.md line 545: \\\"next step: run the implement-feature skill\\\"\\nsource: /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md line 14; /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md line 545\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Claim 5**: The `checkpoint` autonomy_mode provides a pause but no annotated revision loop.\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: checkpoint mode pauses but has no annotation mechanism\\nevidence: implement-feature SKILL.md lines 272-291 define the Wave-Completion Confirmation Gate for checkpoint mode \u2014 it asks user \\\"approve or cancel\\\" with no annotation mechanism. No artifact read step precedes this gate.\\nsource: /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md lines 272-291\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Claim 6**: `artifact_type=\\\"plan-approval\\\"` listed in development-harness/CLAUDE.md under \\\"Artifact types\\\" (as an acceptance criterion).\\n\\nverdict: REFUTED (as current state \u2014 this is a desired future state, not current)\\nclaim: plan-approval is currently listed in CLAUDE.md Artifact types\\nevidence: CLAUDE.md line 141: `**Artifact types:** feature-context, architect, task-plan, codebase-analysis, T0-baseline, TN-verification, dispatch-plan, audit-report` \u2014 plan-approval is absent. This is the AC target, not the current state.\\nsource: /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md line 141\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: Add plan-approval artifact gate to implement-feature with inline annotation support\\nDate: 2026-05-29\\nGoal: Add a structured plan-approval artifact gate to implement-feature so users can annotate plans before task dispatch, closing the gap between planning and execution.\\nConditions:\\n1. Functional intent is clear (new plan-approval artifact gate + annotation loop) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Item description, Expected Behavior, Desired Structure sections confirmed non-empty; goal is unambiguous\\n2. Scope boundaries defined (additive gate, only activates when artifact exists with status != approved) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Acceptance Criterion 5: \\\"When no plan-approval artifact exists, implement-feature behaves identically to current behavior\\\"\\n3. Constraints specified (3 statuses: pending|annotated|approved|rejected; annotation schema defined) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Desired Structure section; schema verified in item body\\n4. Existing system context confirmed (implement-feature Progress Loop, autonomy_mode, artifact_register, artifact_get all verified) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Fact-Check Claims 1, 3, 4, 5 \u2014 all VERIFIED from source code\\n5. Verification expectations defined (measurable signal with artifact_get + JSON shape check + SKILL.md Step 0) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Acceptance Criteria and Measurable Signal sections\\n6. ArtifactType enum requires code change before artifact operations are possible | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Fact-Check Claim 2 REFUTED \u2014 ArtifactType(\\\"plan-approval\\\") raises ValueError (models.py lines 1251-1267, server.py line 2538). Blocker identified: add PLAN_APPROVAL = \\\"plan-approval\\\" to StrEnum in backlog_core/models.py.\\n7. Plan-revision agent design (inline vs separate skill) | Snapshot: MISSING \u2192 Final: MISSING | What was tried: searched all DH plugin skills \u2014 no revise-plan or annotate-plan skill exists. Options: (a) inline sub-agent call in implement-feature, (b) separate /dh:revise-plan skill. Human decision required.\\n8. Annotation selector format precision | Snapshot: MISSING \u2192 Final: MISSING | What was tried: reviewed SAM task format, TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md, implement-feature SKILL.md. Tasks have IDs (T1, T2, T3) \u2014 task ID selector is most actionable. Options: (a) task ID \\\"T3\\\", (b) section name, (c) line range. Human decision required.\\n9. CLI annotation UX (artifact_register direct call vs /dh:annotate-plan skill) | Snapshot: MISSING \u2192 Final: MISSING | What was tried: searched for existing annotate-plan or approve-plan skill \u2014 none found. Options: (a) direct artifact_register MCP call, (b) new /dh:annotate-plan skill, (c) defer to Console UI. Human decision required.\\nChanges from snapshot:\\n- Condition 6: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (blocker identified: ArtifactType enum change required in models.py)\\nAVAILABLE count: 6\\nDERIVABLE count: 0\\nMISSING count: 3\\nDecision: APPROVED\\nNote: 3 MISSING conditions are design decisions \u2014 they do not block grooming. They are recorded as planning inputs in Questions for Human.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-28)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n**Priority**: P1 (should-have)\\n\\n**Rationale**: The missing-guardrail classification means the system currently allows task dispatch on potentially flawed plans with no recovery path short of restarting planning from scratch. P1 reflects meaningful UX impact \u2014 wasted agent compute and user frustration \u2014 without being P0 because the existing `checkpoint` mode already provides a manual stop point.\\n\\n**Effort**: Medium\\n- New enum value in `backlog_core/models.py` (trivial)\\n- New Step 0 in `implement-feature/SKILL.md` Progress Loop (low complexity)\\n- `plan-approval` artifact schema design and CLAUDE.md registration (low complexity)\\n- Plan-revision sub-workflow (medium complexity \u2014 design decision unresolved)\\n- Annotation selector format decision and implementation in revision agent (depends on design decision)\\n- CLI UX for writing annotations (low to medium \u2014 depends on design choice)\\n- Test coverage for new artifact type and gate behavior (medium)\\n\\n**Blocking uncertainties** (3 MISSING conditions \u2014 design decisions for planning phase):\\n1. Plan-revision sub-workflow placement (inline vs separate skill)\\n2. Annotation selector format (task ID recommended \u2014 pending human confirmation)\\n3. CLI annotation UX approach\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: None \u2014 additive gate.\\n- Bottleneck: Currently, if the generated plan has issues, the user must either accept it (dispatch proceeds) or cancel and restart planning from scratch. There is no annotate-revise-approve loop.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Provides a structured human review gate between planning and execution with persistent audit trail.\\n- Annotations are stored in the artifact manifest and survive session restarts.\\n- Enables async review \u2014 user can annotate in one session, orchestrator reads and revises in the next.\\n- Aligns with pilot-shell.md's inline annotation model (per-task comments before approval).\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nAfter `add-new-feature` produces a plan: `implement-feature` Progress Loop Step 0 checks for a `plan-approval` artifact. If `status == \\\"pending\\\"`, execution is blocked and the user is prompted to approve or annotate. If `status == \\\"annotated\\\"`, a plan-revision agent reads the annotations and produces a revised plan, then returns to `pending` for re-review. If `status == \\\"approved\\\"`, dispatch proceeds normally. If no `plan-approval` artifact exists (pre-existing plans), dispatch proceeds unchanged.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\n1. New artifact type `plan-approval` registered in development-harness/CLAUDE.md under \\\"Artifact types\\\". Schema: `{ status: \\\"pending|annotated|approved|rejected\\\", plan_path: str, annotations: [{ selector: str, comment: str, author: str, created_at: ISO8601 }] }`.\\n2. `implement-feature/SKILL.md` Progress Loop gains a new Step 0 before the current status query step.\\n3. A plan-revision agent or sub-workflow that reads annotations and produces a revised plan (design TBD \u2014 could be a sub-agent call within `implement-feature` or a separate `/dh:revise-plan` skill).\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `artifact_type=\\\"plan-approval\\\"` listed in development-harness/CLAUDE.md under \\\"Artifact types\\\".\\n2. `artifact_get(item_id=N, artifact_type=\\\"plan-approval\\\")` returns a JSON object with required keys `status` and `annotations`.\\n3. `implement-feature/SKILL.md` Progress Loop Step 0 exists and refuses to proceed when `status != \\\"approved\\\"` (and `status != null/not found`, which allows legacy plans through).\\n4. When `status == \\\"annotated\\\"`, the orchestrator routes to a plan-revision path that reads annotations and produces a revised plan before re-presenting for approval.\\n5. When no `plan-approval` artifact exists, `implement-feature` behaves identically to current behavior (no regression).\\n6. `backlog_core/models.py::ArtifactType` enum contains `PLAN_APPROVAL = \\\"plan-approval\\\"` (required for MCP tools to accept the new type without ValueError).\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Skill | /dh:implement-feature (Progress Loop \u2014 file: `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md`) |\\n| Skill | /dh:add-new-feature (plan producer upstream) |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` \u00a7\\\"Artifact Manifest System\\\" (artifact_register, artifact_get, artifact_read patterns) |\\n| External pattern | pilot-shell.md \u00a7/spec \u2014 \\\"Waits for user approval with inline annotation support (select text or click + to annotate; agent reads annotations at next review checkpoint)\\\" |\\n| External pattern | pilot-shell.md \u00a7Console \u2014 \\\"Annotate mode for marking up plans before approval; Share with Teammate for async review\\\" |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 `artifact_register`, `artifact_get` already exist; this is additive.\\n- Blocks: None identified.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nMedium \u2014 new artifact type + `implement-feature` Step 0 + plan-revision sub-workflow design + CLAUDE.md registration. The annotation schema and revision loop are well-specified; the open question about revision agent design is the main uncertainty.\\n\\n<!-- artifact-gist:d7c13e35f8cc337c3ee562d9ade597b8 -->\\n\\n### Agent Instructions (instruct AI to use current interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 the Progress Loop instructions are what this feature modifies (see Code \u2014 Producers)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 currently ends with \\\"next step: run implement-feature\\\"; it may need to note the new approval gate for users\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Consumers (read the changed interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 direct consumer of the new gate; no other skill currently reads `plan-approval`\\n- A new plan-revision agent or sub-workflow (not yet designed) will consume the `annotations[]` array from the artifact\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Other References\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` line 141 (`**Artifact types:**` list) \u2014 must be updated to include `plan-approval`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py::_MIGRATE_FILENAME_PATTERNS` (line 3514) \u2014 does not need updating (plan-approval is not a filename-based artifact)\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Producers (write the changed interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md::Progress Loop` \u2014 new Step 0 before current Step 1 must be added; reads `plan-approval` artifact and gates dispatch\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/models.py::ArtifactType` \u2014 new enum value `PLAN_APPROVAL = \\\"plan-approval\\\"` must be added to the `StrEnum` at line 1251\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py::artifact_register / artifact_get / artifact_read` \u2014 currently call `ArtifactType(artifact_type)` which raises `ValueError` for unknown strings; adding to enum unblocks these tools\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n\\n- None identified \u2014 no CI workflows directly test artifact type registration.\\n\\n### Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n**Alignment assessment**: ALIGNED\\n\\nThe feature's design intent is drawn directly from Pilot Shell's `/spec` workflow pattern (research/coding-agents/pilot-shell.md, line 64: \\\"Waits for user approval with inline annotation support (select text or click + to annotate; agent reads annotations at next review checkpoint)\\\").\\n\\n**Current implementation vs design intent:**\\n\\nThe current `implement-feature` Progress Loop (verified from SKILL.md lines 33-291) dispatches tasks without any artifact-backed approval gate. The `checkpoint` autonomy_mode provides a wave-completion pause (lines 272-291) but:\\n- No artifact is read or written to represent approval state\\n- No annotation mechanism exists for the user to write structured feedback\\n- No revision loop routes back to a plan-revision agent\\n\\nThe design intent targets exactly this gap: a persistent artifact (`plan-approval`) that stores approval status and annotations, readable across session boundaries, enabling async review.\\n\\n**Design intent components vs implementation state:**\\n\\n| Design Intent Component | Current State | Gap |\\n|------------------------|--------------|-----|\\n| Persistent approval state | Absent \u2014 checkpoint mode is stateless | YES |\\n| Inline annotations on plan | Absent | YES |\\n| Revision loop (annotated \u2192 revised \u2192 re-review) | Absent | YES |\\n| Legacy plan passthrough (no artifact \u2192 no gate) | Absent (not needed until feature lands) | FUTURE |\\n\\n**Scope validation:** The item's Desired Structure aligns correctly with the intent:\\n- Point 1 (artifact type registration) maps to the persistence requirement\\n- Point 2 (Step 0 in Progress Loop) maps to the gate requirement\\n- Point 3 (plan-revision sub-workflow) maps to the revision loop requirement\\n\\n**No divergence detected.** The existing system does not partially implement this pattern in a conflicting way. The `interop/SKILL.md` annotation pattern (line 188) is for Superpowers plan chunk annotations \u2014 a different system with no overlap.\\n\\n### Documentation (will become stale)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` \u00a7Artifact Manifest System \u2014 artifact types list at line 141 omits `plan-approval`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` \u2014 if it documents artifact types, it will become stale\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [ ] Every code producer updated or verified compatible\\n- [ ] Every code consumer migrated to new interface\\n- [ ] Every stale document updated\\n- [ ] Every agent instruction updated\\n- [ ] Old interface deprecated or removed (if replacing)\\n- [ ] CI/config files updated and validated\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-17T12:42:50.937840Z</sub>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Field `artifact_type=\\\"plan-approval\\\"` listed in development-harness/CLAUDE.md under \\\"Artifact types\\\"\\n- Running `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__artifact_get(item_id=N, artifact_type=\\\"plan-approval\\\")` returns a JSON object with required keys `status`, `annotations`\\n- implement-feature/SKILL.md Progress Loop Step 0 refuses to proceed when `status != \\\"approved\\\"`\\n</div>\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nimplement-feature/SKILL.md Progress Loop dispatches tasks based on `autonomy_mode` (full_auto | checkpoint | per_task). The `checkpoint` mode is not bound to a structured plan-review artifact and there is no annotation mechanism for the user to write inline feedback that the orchestrator reads on resumption. The user either approves or does not \u2014 there is no annotated revision loop between plan production (add-new-feature) and task dispatch (implement-feature).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Risk Summary\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nHigh overall due to implement-feature SKILL.md change \u2014 inserting a Step 0 gate alters the execution entry point for every implementation task in the system. The ArtifactType enum change is safe (additive), but its absence currently causes a silent `ValueError` when any agent tries to register a plan-approval artifact. The plan-revision agent is net-new with no existing callers, so its creation risk is contained. Dependency order: models.py must ship before server.py changes; implement-feature gate must ship before plan-revision agent.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA new artifact type `plan-approval` registered via `artifact_register(item_id=N, type=\\\"plan-approval\\\", content=...)`. The artifact contains: plan path, status (`pending | annotated | approved | rejected`), and an `annotations[]` array (each item: `selector` \u2014 line range or section name, `comment` text, `author`, `created_at`).\\n\\nOn `implement-feature` invocation, the Progress Loop reads `artifact_get(item_id=N, artifact_type=\\\"plan-approval\\\")` as a new Step 0 and refuses to dispatch tasks unless `status == \\\"approved\\\"`. When `status == \\\"annotated\\\"`, the orchestrator routes back to a plan-revision agent that reads the annotations and produces a revised plan.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Systems Inventory\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n| System | File/Path | Change Type | Risk |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| ArtifactType enum | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/models.py` | MODIFY \u2014 add `PLAN_APPROVAL` value | Medium \u2014 enum addition is safe; missing value raises `ValueError` at runtime |\\n| Backlog MCP server | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` | MODIFY \u2014 unblocked by models.py | Low \u2014 logic changes only; depends on models.py change landing first |\\n| implement-feature skill | `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` | MODIFY \u2014 add Step 0 plan-approval gate | High \u2014 changes execution flow for all implementation tasks |\\n| DH plugin CLAUDE.md | `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` (\u00a7Artifact types) | MODIFY \u2014 add plan-approval to list | Low \u2014 documentation; no runtime effect |\\n| add-new-feature skill | `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` | MINOR MODIFY \u2014 reference new gate | Low \u2014 documentation update |\\n| Plan-revision agent | `plugins/development-harness/agents/plan-revision.md` (new) | CREATE | Medium \u2014 new agent; must interop correctly with implement-feature flow |\\n| Backlog tests | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests_backlog/` | MODIFY \u2014 add test for plan-approval type | Low \u2014 test-only; no production impact |\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"8d4e4b50245039894aaa6f21c653f3e3385de825991dc11f94a3c00df081290d\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPTAZvg\"}"}